{"name":"NYC Taxi","hex":"#f7b731","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nyc","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Nyanga-li."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["nice"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nyc"},{"term":"taxi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vehicle, usually a car, that may be hired for single journeys by members of the public, particularly one with an automated meter to calculate the fare.","An aircraft used for practicing ground manoeuvres."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move an aircraft on the ground under its own power.","To travel by taxicab."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taxi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Taxis of New York City","blocks":[{"text":"Taxicabs in New York City come in two varieties: yellow and green; they are widely recognizable symbols of the city. Taxis painted yellow are able to pick up passengers anywhere in the five boroughs. Taxis painted apple green, which began to appear in August 2013, are allowed to pick up passengers in Upper Manhattan, the Bronx, Brooklyn, Queens, and Staten Island. Both types have the same fare structure. Taxicabs are operated by private individuals or companies and licensed by the New York City Taxi and Limousine Commission (TLC). It also oversees over 40,000 other for-hire vehicles, including \"black cars\", commuter vans, and ambulettes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Taxicabs_of_New_York_City.jpg/330px-Taxicabs_of_New_York_City.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxis_of_New_York_City","wikidata":"Q1316596"},{"title":"New York City","blocks":[{"text":"New York, often called New York City (NYC), is the most populous city in the United States. It is located at the southern tip of New York State on New York Harbor, one of the world's largest natural harbors. The city comprises five boroughs—Manhattan, Brooklyn, Queens, the Bronx, and Staten Island—each being coextensive with its respective county. It is the geographical and demographic center of both the Northeast megalopolis and the New York metropolitan area, the largest metropolitan area in the United States by both population and urban area. New York is a global center of technology, finance and commerce, culture, entertainment and media, academics and scientific output, the arts and fashion—and as home to the headquarters of the United Nations, international diplomacy. New York City is known for its fast pace and continuous urban energy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-View_of_Empire_State_Building_from_Rockefeller_Center_New_York_City_dllu_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_City","wikidata":"Q60"},{"title":"Taxi","blocks":[{"text":"A taxi, also known as a taxicab or simply a cab, is a vehicle for hire that provides point-to-point transportation for passengers typically on an exclusive, non-shared basis. This differs from public transport, where pick-up and drop-off points are set by the service provider, although demand-responsive transport and share taxis provide hybrid bus/taxi modes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/TAXI.jpg/330px-TAXI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxi","wikidata":"Q82650"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Car_service_outside_the_Staten_Island_Mall_in_Staten_Island%2C_New_York.JPG/330px-Car_service_outside_the_Staten_Island_Mall_in_Staten_Island%2C_New_York.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Car_service_outside_the_Staten_Island_Mall_in_Staten_Island%2C_New_York.JPG/330px-Car_service_outside_the_Staten_Island_Mall_in_Staten_Island%2C_New_York.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A livery car on Richmond Avenue in Staten Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACar_service_outside_the_Staten_Island_Mall_in_Staten_Island%2C_New_York.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/USACab.JPG/500px-USACab.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/USACab.JPG/1280px-USACab.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/USACab.JPG/500px-USACab.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"New York medallion taxicab in a prior livery. The medallion number is on the side of the taxicab.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AUSACab.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1990-1126-500%2C_Kraftdroschke.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1990-1126-500%2C_Kraftdroschke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1990-1126-500%2C_Kraftdroschke.jpg/500px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_183-1990-1126-500%2C_Kraftdroschke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This ca. 1904 Columbia Hansom Cab is similar to the 1890s E.V.C. cabs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABundesarchiv_Bild_183-1990-1126-500%2C_Kraftdroschke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Old_checker_cab.jpg/500px-Old_checker_cab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/w